---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Home | Open Replicant">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="splash">
      <div class="orb orb--a" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="orb orb--b" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero__content">
      <span class="badge badge--open-source">Open Source AI · Apache-2.0</span>
      <h1>Open Replicant</h1>
      <p class="hero__tagline">
        Infrastructure that manages itself — with you holding the pen. Morphogen
        watches your systems through a veil of telemetry, proposes each fix with
        a stated prediction, and carries nothing out until you approve. Then it
        checks whether the world matched the prophecy.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a href="/product/" class="btn btn--large">View the product</a>
        <a href="/services/" class="btn btn--outline btn--large">Hire us</a>
        <a href="/contribute/" class="btn btn--ghost btn--large">Contribute</a>
        <a href="/saas/" class="btn btn--ghost btn--large">SaaS waitlist</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>What we do</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Open source product</h3>
        <p>
          Morphogen is open source AI infrastructure (Apache-2.0). Self-host it.
          Audit the knowledge kernel. Extend it. The roadmap belongs to the
          community, not a vendor.
        </p>
        <a href="/product/" class="btn btn--ghost">Learn more</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Consulting &amp; implementation</h3>
        <p>
          We help teams deploy Morphogen in production — from system mapping
          through rollout and ongoing support. Systems are described, not
          hand-built. You approve before anything runs.
        </p>
        <a href="/services/" class="btn btn--ghost">Learn more</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>SaaS coming soon</h3>
        <p>
          A managed, hosted Morphogen so you can build, not operate. Join the
          waitlist for early access — export your kernel and self-host anytime.
          No lock-in.
        </p>
        <a href="/saas/" class="btn btn--ghost">Join waitlist</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 2rem;">
    <h2>How Morphogen works</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Observe</h3>
        <p>
          Telemetry flows into the knowledge kernel as attributed claims. Every
          observation cites its source, scored for belief. Nothing is assumed;
          everything is traced.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Analyse</h3>
        <p>
          The analyser weighs anomalies against the system map and raises a
          governed proposal — never a surprise change, never a silent rewrite.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Plan &amp; verify</h3>
        <p>
          The planner proposes a fix with a stated prediction. You review and
          approve in the review lane. After it runs, the verifier checks whether
          the prediction held. The loop closes with evidence.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
